CodeAssist plugin SPI linking exception
=======================================

CodeAssist as a whole is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3
or later, as stated in LICENSE. This file adds a linking exception that applies to
the plugin SPI only, so that a plugin does not have to adopt the IDE's license.

The exception covers exactly these two modules, and nothing else in this
repository:

  * plugin-api    (published as io.github.tyron12233:plugin-api)
  * platform-core (published as io.github.tyron12233:platform-core)

Every source file covered by the exception carries the SPDX identifier

  GPL-3.0-or-later WITH Classpath-exception-2.0

and the exception is the standard Classpath exception, version 2.0, reproduced
below. In practical terms: a CodeAssist plugin that compiles against these two
modules and is loaded into the IDE may be released under any license, including a
proprietary one. Modifying the two modules themselves is still governed by the
GPL, as is the rest of CodeAssist.

